        "step_number": 2,
        "text": "Step 2: Use the angle sum property in triangle $PQS$.\nThe sum of the interior angles in any triangle is $180^\\circ$. In triangle $PQS$, we know $\\angle P = 40^\\circ$ and $\\angle QSR = 35^\\circ$. Let $\\angle QPS = x$. Then,\n\\[x + 40^\\circ + 35^\\circ = 180^\\circ.\\]"
