  "raw_text": "Step 1: Identify the angles related to the parallel lines and transversal.\nSince $\\overline{ST} \\parallel \\overline{QR}$ and $\\overline{SP}$ is a transversal, $\\angle Q$ and $\\angle QSR$ are corresponding angles. Therefore, $\\angle QSR = \\angle Q = 35^\\circ$.\n\nStep 2: Use the angle sum property in triangle $PQS$.\nThe sum of the interior angles in any triangle is $180^\\circ$. In triangle $PQS$, we know $\\angle P = 40^\\circ$ and $\\angle QSR = 35^\\circ$. Let $\\angle QPS = x$. Then,\n\\[x + 40^\\circ + 35^\\circ = 180^\\circ.\\]\n\nStep 3: Solve for $\\angle QPS$.\n\\[x + 75^\\circ = 180^\\circ,\\]\n\\[x = 180^\\circ - 75^\\circ = 105^\\circ.\\]\nSo, $\\angle QPS = 105^\\circ$.\n\nStep 4: Recognize that $\\angle STR$ is the same as $\\angle QPS$ because they are vertically opposite angles.\nTherefore, $\\angle STR = 105^\\circ$.\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{105}$<|im_end|>",
